{"id": "29393", "revid": "162256", "url": "https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki?curid=29393", "title": "Redhill", "text": "\"For other places with the same name, see (disambiguation).\"\nRedhill is a town in the county of Surrey, England. Whilst the town is a hub in commercial terms, with a shopping centre and several offices of large companies, a large proportion of the working population commute to Greater London and other parts of Surrey.\nGet in.\nBy train.\nThere a regular train services to, including trains from London Bridge, London Victoria and Brighton.\nBy plane.\nThe town is close to London Gatwick ().\nGet around.\nThis small town can easily be traversed on foot. However there are plenty of buses local buses (May 2024 Metrobus timetable) Taxis are also readily available.\nSee.\nThere are no real historic sights here.\nThere is a large park in the town centre which can be nice in the summer, however can sometimes get rowdy in the evening.\nBuy.\nTypical high-street names such as Sainsburys, Iceland, Wilkinsons, New Look and Boots in the town centre.\nLearn.\nEast Surrey College, the main college for this area of Surrey. About 15 - 20 minutes walk up the main street from the town centre.\nDrink.\nThe town centre has a few clubs exist in the town centre and some pubs, including a JD Wetherspoon.\nGo next.\nEpsom and London are both nearby. \nNeighboring Reigate could be an option to while away a few hours, and has a good range of pubs and restaurants. "}
